# Structa Cloud – Monorepo

A comprehensive Django monorepo with multiple sites, shared assets, local libraries, and centralized deployment orchestration.

## 🏗️ Project Structure

```
structa.cloud/
├── applications/              # Main Django monorepo
│   ├── Makefile              # Master dispatcher for Django work
│   ├── configs/              # Shared Django configuration
│   │   ├── base/             # Base settings modules
│   │   ├── settings/         # Environment-specific settings
│   │   └── tests/            # Test configuration
│   ├── assets/               # Shared frontend assets
│   │   ├── templates/        # Shared template components
│   │   ├── static/           # Shared static files (CSS, JS, images)
│   │   ├── locale/           # Shared translations
│   │   └── scripts/          # Frontend build scripts
│   ├── www/                  # Shared Django application code
│   ├── libs/                 # Local reusable libraries
│   │   ├── django-fusion/    # Component system + framework tools
│   │   └── ceptor-ai/        # AI/ML integration library
│   ├── scripts/              # Shared automation scripts
│   ├── ctc-research/         # CTC Research site
│   │   ├── plugins/          # Site-specific plugins
│   │   ├── assets/           # Site-specific assets
│   │   └── www/              # Site-specific Django apps
│   ├── lms-demo/             # LMS Demo site
│   ├── VResume/              # VResume portfolio site
│   └── crm/                  # CRM site (optional)
├── proxy/                    # Traefik reverse proxy + SSL
│   ├── traefik/              # Traefik configuration
│   ├── certs/                # SSL certificates
│   └── Makefile              # Proxy deployment commands
├── databases/                # PostgreSQL + Redis
│   ├── docker-compose.yml
│   └── Makefile              # Database deployment commands
├── services/                 # Supporting services (media, monitoring)
│   ├── docker-compose.media.yml
│   └── Makefile              # Service commands
├── compose/                  # Central orchestration
│   ├── docker-compose.applications.yml
│   ├── docker-compose.docs.yml
│   └── docker-compose.tasks.yml
├── docs/                     # Documentation
│   ├── infrastructure/
│   ├── deployment/
│   ├── websites/
│   └── index.html            # Docsify documentation site
├── docker-compose.yml        # Root composition file (includes all)
├── Makefile                  # Root deployment dispatcher
├── DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md       # Complete deployment guide
├── AGENTS.md                 # AI agent instructions + architecture
└── PROMPTS.md                # AI prompt templates

# Canonical sites
applications/ctc-research/   → https://ctc-research.com
applications/lms-demo/       → https://structa-demo.com
applications/VResume/        → https://vresume.structa.cloud
```

## 🚀 Quick Start – Deployment

### Prerequisites

- Docker & Docker Compose
- Python 3.11+ (for local development)
- uv (Python package manager) – optional for versioning

### Deploy Everything

```bash
# Full deployment with validation (postgres-first order)
make deploy

# Or: deploy specific components
make deploy-databases        # PostgreSQL + Redis
make deploy-app              # All Django applications
make deploy-proxy            # Traefik reverse proxy
make deploy-media            # Nginx media server
```

### Monitor Deployment

```bash
# Check status of all services
make status

# View logs from all services
make logs

# Follow Coolify logs (streaming)
make logs-common
```

## 📋 Make Commands Reference

### Commands Tree

```
make
├── deploy                   # Full deployment (postgres-first order)
│   ├── deploy-databases     # PostgreSQL + Redis
│   ├── deploy-media         # Nginx media server
│   ├── deploy-app           # All Django applications
│   ├── deploy-tasks         # Celery background workers
│   ├── deploy-docs          # Documentation site
│   └── deploy-proxy         # Traefik reverse proxy
├── deploy-ci                # CI validation (no deploy)
├── deploy-preflight         # Smoke-test compose files
├── preflight-network        # Validate Docker network names
├── create-networks          # Create required Docker networks
├── status                   # Show deployment status
├── logs                     # Show logs from all services
├── stop                     # Stop all services
├── restart                  # Restart all services (= stop + deploy)
├── prune                    # Remove stopped containers, volumes, and images
├── clean                    # Aggressive teardown (containers, volumes, images)
├── build                    # Build all component images
├── build-app                # Build Django application images
├── push                     # Push repo + lib submodules to origin
├── pull                     # Fetch + smart-merge origin into current branch
├── sync                     # Pull then push in one step
├── ctc-research             # Delegate to applications/Makefile (WEBSITE=ctc-research)
├── lms-demo                 # Delegate to applications/Makefile (WEBSITE=lms-demo)
├── vresume                  # Delegate to applications/Makefile (WEBSITE=vresume)
├── help                     # Show main command reference
└── help-all                 # Show extended + component-specific help
```

See **[AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md#Deployment--Make-Commands)** for the full commands reference.

### Main Deployment

```bash
make deploy                  # Full deployment (databases → apps → proxy)
make deploy-ci              # CI validation (no deploy)
make deploy-preflight       # Smoke-test compose files
make preflight-network      # Validate network configuration

# Component deployments
make deploy-app             # Django applications (all sites)
make deploy-proxy           # Traefik reverse proxy
make deploy-media           # Nginx media server
make deploy-tasks           # Celery background workers
make deploy-docs            # Documentation site
make deploy-databases       # PostgreSQL + Redis
make deploy-coder           # Coder IDE platform
make deploy-customizer      # Template customizer
```

### Management

```bash
make status                 # Show deployment status
make logs                   # Show service logs
make stop                   # Stop all services
make restart                # Restart all services
make create-networks        # Create Docker networks
```

### Cleanup

```bash
make prune                  # Remove containers + volumes + images
make prune-containers       # Remove stopped containers
make prune-volumes          # Remove unused volumes
make prune-images           # Remove unused images
make clean                  # Aggressive teardown
```

### Per-Site Shortcuts

```bash
make ctc-research          # CTC Research site commands
make lms-demo              # LMS Demo site commands
make vresume               # VResume site commands
```

### Git & Versioning

```bash
make push                  # Push to origin + submodules
make pull                  # Pull from origin
make sync                  # Pull then push
make bump-app-patch        # Bump applications version
```

See **[DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md](./DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md)** and **[AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md)** for complete command reference.

## 🏢 Sites & Applications

### CTC Research – `applications/ctc-research/`

- **URL**: https://ctc-research.com
- **Port (local)**: 5070
- **Type**: Django + Wagtail CMS
- **Key Features**: Blog, LMS, Learning paths

### LMS Demo – `applications/lms-demo/`

- **URL**: https://structa-demo.com
- **Port (local)**: 5071
- **Type**: Django + Wagtail CMS
- **Key Features**: Learning management, courses, payments

### VResume – `applications/VResume/`

- **URL**: https://vresume.structa.cloud
- **Port (local)**: 5072
- **Type**: Django + Portfolio builder
- **Key Features**: Portfolio, resume builder, AI-powered

## 📚 Shared Libraries

### django-fusion (`applications/libs/django-fusion/`)

**Import**: `from django_fusion import ...`

Unified component system + framework tools:
- `{% comp %}` template tag for reusable components
- Model viewsets, routing, generic CBVs
- Form handling, tables, pagination
- Site layer abstractions

**Documentation**: See `/applications/libs/django-fusion/docs/`

### ceptor-ai (`applications/libs/ceptor-ai/`)

**Import**: `from ceptor_ai import ...`

AI/ML integration and utilities:
- Contact, team, organization management
- Email & CRM integration
- Tag system and analytics

**Documentation**: See `/applications/libs/ceptor-ai/` README

## 🔧 Configuration

### Shared Settings

All sites inherit from `applications/configs/`:

```python
# Base configuration (inherited by all sites)
from applications.configs.base.templates import TEMPLATES
from applications.configs.base.auth import AUTH_SETTINGS
from applications.configs.base.cache import CACHE_CONFIG

# Site-specific overrides in applications/<site>/settings.py
```

### Template Resolution Order

1. Site templates: `applications/<site>/templates/`
2. Site plugins: `applications/<site>/plugins/templates/`
3. Shared templates: `applications/assets/templates/`
4. Site-specific plugins: `applications/<site>/plugins/`

## 🌐 Infrastructure

### Networks

```
common          # Default service network
traefik-net     # Proxy network
internal        # Internal-only services
utilities-net   # Monitoring
warehouse-net   # Data warehouse
ollama-net      # AI/ML services
```

### Services

```
Proxy           → localhost:443 (Traefik, HTTPS)
CTC Research    → localhost:5070
LMS Demo        → localhost:5071
VResume         → localhost:5072
Media Server    → localhost:8080 (Nginx)
PostgreSQL      → localhost:5432
Redis           → localhost:6379
```

