## 🛠️ Common Workflows

### Deploy CTC Research After Changes

```bash
# 1. Option A: Redeploy via Make
make ctc-research docker-up

# 2. Option B: Full redeploy via root Make
make deploy-app

# 3. Option C: Full deployment with preflight
make deploy
```

### View Site Logs

```bash
# CTC Research logs
docker logs ctc-research-website --tail 50 -f

# LMS Demo logs
docker logs lms-demo-website --tail 50 -f

# VResume logs
docker logs vresume-website --tail 50 -f

# Or use Make
make logs
```

### Add a New Django Model to CTC Research

```bash
# 1. Add model to applications/ctc-research/plugins/blog/models.py
# 2. Create migration
make ctc-research makemigrations

# 3. Run migration
make ctc-research migrate

# 4. Create or update templates/serializers as needed
# 5. Update tests if applicable
```

### Add a Shared Template Component

```bash
# 1. Create in applications/assets/templates/components/
#    e.g., applications/assets/templates/components/cards/contact_card.html

# 2. Use in templates:
#    {% load components %}
#    {% comp "components/cards/contact_card.html" contact=contact / %}

# 3. Document in applications/assets/templates/components/AGENTS.md
```

## 🧪 Testing

```bash
# Run all tests
make -C applications test

# Run tests for specific site
make ctc-research test WEBSITE=ctc-research

# Run specific test file
make -C applications test-file WEBSITE=ctc-research TEST_FILE=path/to/test.py
```

## 🔐 Environment Variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in:

```bash
# Django
DEBUG=False
SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here

# Databases
POSTGRES_DB=structa
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your-postgres-password

# Email
EMAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
EMAIL_PORT=587
EMAIL_HOST_USER=your-email@example.com
EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD=your-email-password

# AWS S3 (optional)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-access-key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret-key

# GitHub (for `make push`)
github=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxx  # Or: export GITHUB_TOKEN=
```

